    <statement><p>Compute implicit derivatives of the following expressions</p>
<p>Write <m>y'</m> for <m>\frac{dy}{dx}</m>.</p>
<p><alert> A.</alert> <m>\quad \frac{d}{dx} \displaystyle \Biggl[4y-\left(4+4x\right)\Biggr] =</m>
<fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p><alert> B.</alert> <m>\quad \frac{d}{dx} \displaystyle \Biggl[x^{2}y+y\Biggr] =</m>
<fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
<p><alert> C.</alert> <m>\quad \frac{d}{dx} \displaystyle \Biggl[\frac{y+4}{x-1}\Biggr] =</m>
<fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
<p><alert> D.</alert> <m>\quad \frac{d}{dx} \displaystyle \Biggl[e^{x^{3}+y^{3}}\Biggr] =</m>
<fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0004"/></p>
<p><alert> E.</alert> <m>\quad \frac{d}{dx} \displaystyle \Biggl[\ln\mathopen{}\left(x^{2}y\right)\Biggr] =</m>
<fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0005"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>4y'-4</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>2xy+x^{2}y'+y'</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{y'\mathopen{}\left(x-1\right)-\left(y+4\right)}{\left(x-1\right)^{2}}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\left(3x^{2}+3y^{2}y'\right)e^{x^{3}+y^{3}}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{2}{x}+\frac{y'}{y}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
